{
  "name": "G11",
  "scenario": "G11: typed input, with no caller speech. A typed message with a text part and an image part, then response.create, starts a typed run, and the backend calls the client's get_menu tool. While the run waits for the output, the client types a second message and asks to continue too early, which is refused with the official function_call_outputs_required. The output and a response.create then continue the run: the continuation carries the output, then the second message. Each typed message enters the talker's memory, so the writer speaks the backend's answer knowing both. (A response.create with nothing queued was once refused first; it is a typed run now, as GPT-Live's reference says.)",
  "tags": [
    {
      "channel": "delegations/<item_1>",
      "contains": {
        "type": "session.delegation.created"
      },
      "row": "GW-20",
      "note": "The typed run is announced without the client_event_id of the response.create that started it (typed_run). B5 announces a typed run with that command's client_event_id (F-1k), so this event gains client_event_id: typed_run."
    },
    {
      "channel": "backend_requests",
      "contains": "What teas do you have?",
      "row": "PV-05",
      "note": "The typed message's input_image part is dropped when the input items become chat messages (FBL:models/chat_completions/translation.py:25,29-35), so both requests carry its text only: the round that starts the typed run and the continuation, which resends the history. B6 sends the image too."
    },
    {
      "channel": "frontend_requests",
      "contains": {
        "max_tokens": 512
      },
      "row": "TK-17",
      "note": "complete_once drops max_output_tokens: the talker's 400 and the writer's 800 never reach their requests, which go out with the sampling default of 512. B11 passes the limits through."
    },
    {
      "channel": "delegations",
      "contains": {
        "event": {
          "type": "response.output_item.added",
          "item": {
            "type": "message"
          }
        }
      },
      "row": "CO-11",
      "note": "The answer message carries no phase. B7 labels every assistant message (final_answer here) and holds a round's text to its end."
    },
    {
      "channel": "delegations",
      "contains": {
        "event": {
          "type": "response.output_item.done",
          "item": {
            "type": "message"
          }
        }
      },
      "row": "CO-11",
      "note": "The completed answer message carries no phase; B7 adds it (final_answer here)."
    }
  ],
